        "title": "Expert Backed Review Summary",
        "text": "<p>Nutricost Pure L-Citrulline Powder distinguishes itself through simplicity and value. Unlike citrulline malate products, it contains pure L-citrulline without added malic acid, providing 3 grams per serving and allowing users to adjust dosing according to their training goals. Research suggests L-citrulline may support nitric oxide production, potentially enhancing blood flow, exercise endurance, and perceived muscle pump during workouts. The formula is gluten-free, non-GMO, vegetarian-friendly, and manufactured in a GMP-compliant, FDA-registered facility with third-party testing claims. Users frequently praise its affordability, large serving count, and effectiveness when used before resistance training or intense exercise. Many also appreciate the absence of artificial flavors and stimulants. However, the unflavored powder isn't entirely taste-neutral. Some reviewers describe a bitter taste and occasional mixing inconsistencies that require extra shaking or warmer liquids for better dissolution. Community discussions also highlight concerns about batch-to-batch texture differences, though many long-term users continue reporting satisfactory results.</p>",
